          },
          "s9": {
            "id": "s9",
            "doc_id": "hotpotqa:1000",
            "start": 725,
            "end": 1053,
            "text": "Among the most commonly traded goods were Jade, obsidian, chocolate, honey, feathers, chewing gum, and salt. It is believed that throughout much of its history, Muyil had strong ties to the center of Coba located some 44 km the north / northwest. The 2010 federal census reported a population of 191 inhabitants in the locality.",
